  "notes": "Kaiser Permanente San Francisco Mission Bay Medical Offices, 1600 Owens St -- a 9-to-10-story outpatient medical office building (sources disagree: STUDIOS Architecture's own project page says nine stories with 220,000 sq ft; Potrero View and the DataSF Assessor tax roll both say 10 stories, tax roll property_area 250,884 sq ft, likely including garage/below-grade area; Kaiser's own reporting and Potrero View cite 200,000 sq ft) with primary care, OB/GYN, pediatrics, dermatology, orthopedics, optical and occupational health -- no emergency department. Built speculatively by developer/fee-manager Alexandria Real Estate Equities, architect STUDIOS Architecture, design-build general contractor Whiting-Turner; Kaiser Foundation Health Plan, Inc. purchased the building outright from Alexandria for approximately \u0005.2M in a sale that closed Dec 20, 2013 (Alexandria's own SEC earnings-supplemental filing), so Kaiser owns the real estate rather than leasing it. Completed 2016; opened to patients March 2016. LEED rating also disputed (STUDIOS claims Platinum; Potrero View says Gold) and left unresolved. Blklot 8709020 confirmed via DataSF's Assessor Parcels dataset and Historical Secured Property Tax Roll (property_location '1600 OWENS ST', use_code COMO/property_class OMD, year_property_built 2016); zoning_district 'MISSION BAY REDEVELOPMENT' (MB-RA) in data/raw/parcels.geojson confirms the Mission Bay South project area.",
